The logic would depend on the specific requirements of your application, but here's an example of how you might do it:

```java
public boolean isFormListed(Document doc) {
    Element form = doc.selectFirst("form");
    return form != null;
}

public boolean isFormSubmittable(Document doc) {
    Element form = doc.selectFirst("form");
    if (form == null) {
        return false;
    }
    String action = form.attr("action");
    if (!action.isEmpty()) {
        return true;
    } else {
        return false;
    }
}
```

This code checks if there is a `form` element in the document, and if so, returns whether it has an `action` attribute. If the `action` attribute is not empty, the form is considered submittable.
